    "final_answer": "Upgraded `settlement_reconcile.py` from the v1 GraphQL API to v2.\n\nChanges:\n- Switched to `POST /v2/graphql` with the paginated `Settlements` query.\n- Follows `pageInfo.endCursor` while `hasNextPage` is true, including short and empty pages.\n- Deduplicates by `id` and keeps the **last delivered version**, since amended settlements are re-delivered.\n- Retries `429` responses using `Retry-After`, resending the identical query, operation, and variables.\n- Restarts safely from the beginning on an invalid/expired cursor.\n\nVerification against `http://the VM's public address:18081`:\n- **1,873 settlements** written, all unique.\n- Output matched the live v1 ledger exactly, including amended values and order.\n- Mock-server test covering empty/short pages, amendments, `429` retries, identical retry requests, and invalid-cursor restart passed with an exact expected match.",
